Z||000009||mshill||05-15-2000||12:08 PM||||I have been getting some parts (engine sensors, EGR Solenoid, Distributor parts) off of 86 Pointiac 6000 SE cars.  Don't know about the heads though.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobertVol||05-15-2000||03:36 PM||||Here are the cars with the 2.8 ...not any order or specs difference<P>Pontiac Firebirds had it as base engine back in the 80's<BR>Pontiac 6000 SE/STE<BR>Pontiac 1988 Grand Prix <BR>Chevy Beretta/Corsica<BR>Chevy blazer<BR>Chevy celebrity<BR>Buick Skylarks sport 2 door<BR>OLDs Firenza--(Remember that one?)<BR>Chevy cavalier z-24<BR>OLDS Cutlass Suprme <BR>Buick Regal<BR>Buick Century<P>I may have missed a few.....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||05-15-2000||03:59 PM||||The Fiero V6 (L44) was only used in the Fiero with that designation.  The Firebird Camaro (LB8) has nearly identical HP/Torque numbers, but vary slightly.  The LB8 hp peak comes 500 RPM higher (4900) and it has 5 less lb-ft of torque (160 @3900 vs 165 @3600 for the L44)||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ozzy||05-15-2000||07:20 PM||||Lottsa good info...<P>To clarify, I don,t expect to find an "exact" same manifold but rather a cast manifold that the bolt holes will line up on. If it is not too wide with respect to the space available between the firewall and engine then the rest would be adaptable. I guess there is also the AC compressor to consider concerning clearance too.<P>I'm sure you Fiero veterans have researched this before...Am I just dreaming for a "No Sprint Header" solution to the V6 exhaust problems?<P>Maybe If I get a welder I could make my own outta steam pipe!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
